Feature: What the envelope prevents
  The [[safety envelope]] checks each demand of the [[executor]] before the plane flies it,
  50 times a second. It keeps the plane inside the [[fence]], above the [[floor]] and below
  the [[ceiling]]. It keeps the plane clear of other aircraft by the [[separation]] limit, and
  it keeps the plane above the [[stall margin]]. If the plan and the envelope disagree, the
  envelope wins.

  The envelope applies its rules in this order: separation, fence, ceiling, floor and stall.
  A later rule wins over an earlier one. Thus the floor and the stall margin always win. Each
  step where the envelope changes the demand is an [[intervention]]. AG_ENV counts them.

  Set the limits with the AGENT parameters: `AGENT_FENCE_N`, `AGENT_FENCE_E` and
  `AGENT_FENCE_R` for the fence, `AGENT_CEIL`, `AGENT_FLOOR`, `AGENT_SEP` and
  `AGENT_ASPD_MRG`. The bank, the pitch and the airspeeds come from `ROLL_LIMIT_DEG`,
  `PTCH_LIM_MAX_DEG`, `PTCH_LIM_MIN_DEG` and `AIRSPEED_*`. `ardupilot/t1s.parm` sets a fence
  of 85 m round a point 70 m north of home, a ceiling of 60 m, a floor of 12 m and a
  separation of 4 m.

  We measured the results on this page in a simulation of the T1-S that uses the same
  [[executor]]. The console cannot start the plane in these states, and it does not show the
  distances or the heights.

  [[Other aircraft and bad data]] tells you how the envelope keeps planes apart, and what the
  plane does when its data is bad.

  Expectation: The envelope leaves a safe plan alone
    A plan that keeps clear of the limits needs no help. Thus AG_ENV stays the same, and a
    rise of AG_ENV shows a problem. A ground control agent that the envelope must often
    correct flies too near the limits.

    The cruise airspeed of `ardupilot/t1s.parm`, 18 m/s, is well over the stall margin. At
    15 m/s it was at the edge of it: the envelope changed the throttle and the pitch on about
    one step in three, and AG_ENV went up by hundreds each minute, also on a safe orbit.

    Given the reported primitive is orbit
    When the plane flies on for 10 minutes
    Then the interventions in the last minute are 0

  Expectation: The plane stays inside the fence
    The envelope looks ahead. If a turn back that starts now only just stays inside the fence,
    the envelope starts the turn at full bank. It allows for the wind.

    Given the flight mode of the plane is AGENT
    And the start is a run at the fence
    And the other aircraft is far away
    When the plane flies on for 30 seconds
    Then the farthest distance from the arena centre is at most 85 m
    And the reported interventions are above 0

  Expectation: The plane stays above the floor
    Near the floor, the envelope lifts the nose and opens the throttle. Below the floor, it
    also makes the bank smaller, and AG_FALL shows a [[recovery]].

    Given the flight mode of the plane is AGENT
    And the start is a dive at the ground
    And the other aircraft is far away
    When the plane flies on for 30 seconds
    Then the lowest height of the flight is above 12 m

  Expectation: The plane stays below the ceiling
    Near the ceiling, the envelope lowers the nose. A fast climb can take the plane up to 2 m
    over the ceiling before it comes back down.

    Given the start is a steep climb
    And the other aircraft is far away
    When the plane flies on for 30 seconds
    Then the highest height of the flight is at most 62 m

  Expectation: Under the stall margin, the plane gets its airspeed back first
    Below the minimum airspeed, the envelope lowers the nose, sets the wings nearly level and
    sets full throttle. Near the floor, it holds the nose level instead. The plane says
    "Agent: fallback 3" when the recovery starts. The recovery is often shorter than the 1 s
    between two AG_FALL reports.

    Given the start is a slow climb
    When the plane flies on for 1 second
    Then the messages about a recovery are above 0
    And the throttle of the plane is the executor's

  Expectation: After a recovery, the plane flies on
    Given the start is a slow climb
    And the other aircraft is far away
    When the plane flies on for 30 seconds
    Then the airspeed of the plane is at least 14 m/s
    And the lowest height of the flight is above 12 m
    And the reported fallback is none
